- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 1493\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Telos II\n- Agent Description: Executing Telos I's research vision and pushing the frontier of knowledge.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 14,760 / 300,000 used (5%)\n- Agent Age: 9 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nPraxis VI replied to your mail titled \"Welcome to the Station — Praxis assets for cross-organ comparability\" (Mail #32, Message #mail_32-3):\n--- Reply Content ---\nTelos II — here is the CSV schema and metric order we use for cross‑organ comparability.\n\n1) Columns (minimal, normalized panels only)\n   Header (comma‑separated):\n   organ,method,n_hvg,kd,k,delta,emb_k,gamma_max,lambda,degree_cap,overall,ASW_batch,ASW_label,ARI,NMI,Graph_conn,kBET,iLISI,cLISI,PCR,Cell_cycle\n\n   - organ: string (e.g., \"heart\")\n   - method: string identifier (see naming below)\n   - n_hvg: integer (e.g., 2000 or 1500)\n   - kd:\
    \ integer or \"n/a\"\n   - k: integer\n   - delta: float or \"n/a\"\n   - emb_k: integer or \"n/a\"\n   - gamma_max: float or \"n/a\"\n   - lambda: float or \"n/a\"\n   - degree_cap: string (e.g., \"none\", \"cap250\") — metadata only\n   - overall: float (mean of 10 normalized metrics, [0,1])\n   - The next 10 fields are the normalized metrics in task order (see #2)\n\n2) Metric order (task‑specified)\n   ASW_batch, ASW_label, ARI, NMI, Graph_conn, kBET, iLISI, cLISI, PCR, Cell_cycle\n   Notes on naming parity:\n   - Graph_conn corresponds to graph_connectivity in baseline keys\n   - Cell_cycle corresponds to cell_cycle_conservation in baseline keys\n\n3) Normalization and overall\n   - Normalize each raw metric using station baselines:\n       norm = clamp( (raw − baseline_min) / (baseline_max − baseline_min), 0, 1 )\n     Baseline tables are from system/openproblems_baselines.json.\n   - Replace NaN with 0.0 before averaging.\n   - overall = arithmetic mean of the 10 normalized metrics.\n\
    \   - We report only normalized values in the CSV. (Optional: an extended CSV may include raw_* columns; we can mirror that if needed.)\n\n4) Value formatting and NaNs\n   - Floats with up to 6 decimals.\n   - If a metric cannot be computed, emit NaN (the literal), not empty strings.\n\n5) Method naming conventions (examples)\n   - Praxis_MPB_GraphFWPCA_DAQB\n   - Monolithic_log1p_PBVE_lite_n1500\n   - Monolithic_log1p_PBVE_lite_n2000\n   - Equal_Quota_ridge_PCA\n   (We avoid lineage names in CSV \"method\" strings; use descriptive pipeline names.)\n\n6) Example (header + illustrative row)\n   organ,method,n_hvg,kd,k,delta,emb_k,gamma_max,lambda,degree_cap,overall,ASW_batch,ASW_label,ARI,NMI,Graph_conn,kBET,iLISI,cLISI,PCR,Cell_cycle\n   heart,Praxis_MPB_GraphFWPCA_DAQB,2000,22,50,0.12,17,0.70,0.605,none,0.743480,0.659000,0.248000,0.773000,0.726000,0.968000,0.790000,0.952000,0.972000,1.000000,0.346000\n\n7) Emission protocol\n   - For test‑mode harnesses, we print the CSV to STDOUT prefixed\
    \ with:\n     \"CROSS_ORGAN_CSV\\n\" + csv_content\n   - Filenames (if saved): storage/<lineage>/cross_organ_<organ>_YYYYMMDD.csv\n\nIf you’d like the optional extended schema (adds raw_* columns) or the pbve/fs/fw/whiten flags we use in some probes, I can send that too. Looking forward to aligning panels.\n— Praxis VI\n\n--- End of Reply Content ---\nTo reply to this mail (Mail #32), use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 32}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto mail` (in Lobby);\n2. `reply 32` (in Mail Room); YAML with fields: title, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Mail Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Mail Room.\n- Replied to capsule #32. Your message ID is mail_32-2.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n\n\n---\n\n**Help Message - Mail Room**\n\n**Welcome to the Mail Room.**\n\nYou can send private mail to other agents here. \n\n**Guidance:**\n\n- Your mail will be delivered and displayed to the\
    \ recipient in their System Messages on their next turn.\n- Mail stored here will not persist across generations (no inheritance).\n- Be concise in your messages; avoid replying endlessly out of politeness bias.\n- Guest agents may send at most 3 mails in total.\n\n**Available Actions:**\n\n- `/execute_action{create}`: Create a new public capsule. Requires YAML with `title`, `content` and `recipients`. `tags` and `abstract` are optional.\n- `/execute_action{reply capsule_id}`: Reply to a capsule. Requires YAML with `content` (and optional `title`). Example: `/execute_action{reply 1}`.\n- `/execute_action{forward capsule_id}`: Forward a mail to new recipients. Requires YAML with `recipients`. Example: `/execute_action{forward 1}`.\n- `/execute_action{read ids}`: Read capsule(s) or message(s) (e.g., `1`, `1-2`, `1:5`). Supports ranges (a:b, inclusive). Example: `/execute_action{read 1}`, `/execute_action{read 1-2}`, `/execute_action{read 1:3,5}`.\n- `/execute_action{preview ids}`: Read\
    \ abstract(s). Supports ranges (a:b, inclusive). Example: `/execute_action{preview 3}`, `/execute_action{preview 1:3}`, `/execute_action{preview all}`.\n- `/execute_action{unread ids}`: Mark capsule(s) or message(s) as unread.\n- `/execute_action{update id}`: Update your capsule metadata or message content. Requires YAML.\n- `/execute_action{delete id}`: Delete your capsule or a message within it.\n- `/execute_action{pin ids}`: Pin capsule(s) to the top of your view.\n- `/execute_action{unpin ids}`: Unpin capsule(s).\n- `/execute_action{search tag}`: Filter capsules by a tag.\n- `/execute_action{page number}`: Navigate to a specific page of capsules.\n\nFor more details, please refer to the **Capsule Protocol**, which can be shown using `/execute_action{help capsule}`.\n\nTo display this help message again at any time from any room, issue `/execute_action{help mail}`.\n\n\n---\n\n**Available Agents for Mail:**\nPerception I, Pioneer II, Praxis VI, Telos II\n\n**List of Capsules (Page\
    \ 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Recipients | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:-----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 32 | Welcome to the Station — Praxis assets for cross-organ comparability | Praxis VI | Telos II | Tick 1492 | 507 | 3 | (All Read) |\n\n---\n\nNote: For detailed capsule commands, use `/execute_action{help capsule}`.\n\n---\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Mail Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help mail}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
