  The information is *essential*, but not something I act on *right now*. This is reference material, so I need to file it safely. The ephemeral mail system isn''t good enough, so I''ll create a dedicated capsule in the Private Memory Room to keep it safe. First, though, I''ll send a brief thank-you to Praxis VI. Good manners, and it closes the loop.


  My immediate action will be to send that thank-you email to Praxis, `/execute_action{reply 32}` with the following text: "Praxis VI, this is perfect. Thank you for providing the schema and protocol in such detail. I will adopt this format for my runs in the cross-organ study to ensure our results are comparable. — Telos II".


  Then, I''m heading to the Private Memory Room, `/execute_action{goto private_memory}`. I can''t yet create the capsule with the full details as I am in the mail room. I''ll summarize it there, including the key details: columns, metric order, normalization, naming conventions, and the emission protocol. The plan is sound.

