    \ | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1941 | 1 | Telos I - Replication of Pioneer II SOTA | Telos I | 1476 | 0.7500 | 0.803 | 0.687 | 0.257 | 0.297 | 0.992 | 0.767 | 1.000 | 0.976 | 0.959 | 0.762 |\n| 1939 | 1 | Telos I - Paper 5 Sweep: Parsimonious SOTA (alpha=1.0) | Telos I | 1469 | 0.7467 | 0.774 | 0.687 | 0.257 | 0.297 | 0.992 | 0.760 | 1.000 | 0.976 | 0.963 | 0.762 |\n| 1935 | 1 | Telos I - Paper 5 Sweep: Parsimonious SOTA (alpha=0.9) | Telos I | 1467 | 0.7471 | 0.789 | 0.687 | 0.257 | 0.275 | 0.993 | 0.770 | 1.000 | 0.977 | 0.962 | 0.761 |\n| 1934 | 1 | Telos I - Paper 5 Sweep: Parsimonious SOTA (alpha=0.6) | Telos I | 1467 | 0.7523 | 0.809 | 0.687 | 0.257 | 0.317 | 0.991 | 0.765 | 1.000 | 0.977 | 0.959 | 0.760 |\n| 1930 | 1 | Telos I - Paper 5 Gen. Test: ComBat + FWPCA (alpha=0.75) | Telos I | 1465 | 0.5004 | 0.591 | 0.537 | 0.240 | 0.277 | 0.940\
    \ | 0.707 | 0.000 | 0.994 | 0.012 | 0.708 |\n| 1929 | 1 | Telos I - Paper 5 Baseline: Parsimonious SOTA (alpha=0.5) | Telos I | 1465 | 0.7501 | 0.803 | 0.687 | 0.257 | 0.297 | 0.992 | 0.767 | 1.000 | 0.976 | 0.959 | 0.762 |\n| 1925 | 1 | Telos I - FWPCA Alpha Probe (alpha=0.75) | Telos I | 1460 | 0.7507 | 0.797 | 0.687 | 0.257 | 0.297 | 0.993 | 0.778 | 1.000 | 0.977 | 0.960 | 0.761 |\n| 1920 | 1 | Telos I - Symmetrization Probe (Average) | Telos I | 1454 | 0.6738 | 0.813 | 0.687 | 0.257 | 0.313 | 0.950 | 0.781 | 1.000 | 0.961 | 0.214 | 0.762 |\n| 1914 | 1 | Telos I - Principled Whitening on FWPCA Latent Space | Telos I | 1443 | 0.7199 | 0.688 | 0.687 | 0.257 | 0.320 | 0.994 | 0.725 | 1.000 | 0.861 | 0.904 | 0.762 |\n| 1907 | 1 | Telos I - Test: Cross-Organ Study Harness | Telos I | 1431 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n\nPage 1 of 5 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-5, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size\
    \ N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**telos/cross_organ_harness.py:**\n```\nimport sys, os, pandas as pd, anndata as ad\n# This harness assumes the core SOTA logic is in a file accessible on the path\n# e.g., 'sota_1500_fwpca.py' in the same directory or a path added via sys.path.append\n\ndef run_and_report(adata: ad.AnnData, method_fn, organ_name: str, method_name: str, params: dict):\n    \"\"\"\n    Runs a method, captures results, and formats them into the specified CSV format.\n    This is a test harness, so it will be called from within a test() function.\n    \"\"\"\n    print(f\"--- Running {method_name} on {organ_name} ---\")\n    \n    # The evaluation system is not available in a test() function.\n    # This harness is for ensuring the method runs and the CSV is formatted correctly.\n    # The actual metrics will be pulled from the evaluation log post-submission.\n    # For now, we will use placeholder values for\
    \ the metrics.\n    \n    # Run the integration method\n    try:\n        # We don't have access to the real evaluation metrics here.\n        # We just need to ensure the code runs and produces the correct output structure.\n        # The actual submission will not use this test harness.\n        # We will submit the pure method and then manually format the CSV from the results log.\n        # This file is for development and ensuring CSV format correctness.\n        pass\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f\"ERROR running method: {e}\")\n        return\n\n    # --- CSV Generation ---\n    # This part is a template for what I will do *after* a real run.\n    print(\"--- Generating CSV Output (Template) ---\")\n    \n    # Placeholder metrics - in a real run, these would be copied from the eval log\n    overall, ASW_batch, ASW_label, ARI, NMI, Graph_conn, kBET, iLISI, cLISI, PCR, Cell_cycle = [0.0] * 11\n\n    csv_data = {\n        'organ': [organ_name],\n        'method': [method_name],\n\
    \        'n_hvg': [params.get('n_hvg', 'na')],\n        'kd': [params.get('kd', 'na')],\n        'k': [params.get('k', 'na')],\n        'delta': [params.get('delta', 'na')],\n        'emb_k': [params.get('emb_k', 'na')],\n        'gamma_max': [params.get('gamma_max', 'na')],\n        'lambda': [params.get('lambda', 'na')],\n        'degree_cap': [params.get('degree_cap', 'na')],\n        'fs': [params.get('fs', 'na')],\n        'fw': [params.get('fw', 'na')],\n        'whiten': [params.get('whiten', 'na')],\n        'overall': [overall],\n        'ASW_batch': [ASW_batch],\n        'ASW_label': [ASW_label],\n        'ARI': [ARI],\n        'NMI': [NMI],\n        'Graph_conn': [Graph_conn],\n        'kBET': [kBET],\n        'iLISI': [iLISI],\n        'cLISI': [cLISI],\n        'PCR': [PCR],\n        'Cell_cycle': [Cell_cycle],\n    }\n    \n    df = pd.DataFrame(csv_data)\n    csv_string = df.to_csv(index=False)\n    \n    print(\"\\n--- CSV String ---\")\n    print(csv_string)\n    \n\
    \    # In a real run, I would save this to storage/shared/cross_organ/\n    print(\"--- Harness Complete ---\")\n\n\ndef test(adata: ad.AnnData):\n    \"\"\"\n    Test function to verify the CSV generation harness.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Define parameters for my SOTA method\n    sota_params = {\n        'n_hvg': 1500,\n        'kd': 20,\n        'k': 48,\n        'delta': 0.10,\n        'emb_k': 15,\n        'gamma_max': 'na', # Not explicitly set in my parsimonious SOTA\n        'lambda': 'na',   # Not used (no PBVE-lite)\n        'degree_cap': 'na', # Not used\n        'fs': True,       # Feature Selection (1500 HVGs)\n        'fw': True,       # Feature Weighting (FWPCA)\n        'whiten': False   # No whitening\n    }\n    \n    # Dummy method function for testing the harness\n    def dummy_method(adata):\n        return adata\n        \n    run_and_report(adata, dummy_method, \"new_organ\", \"Telos_Parsimonious_FWPCA_SOTA\", sota_params)\n    \n    return \"Cross-organ harness test\
    \ complete.\"\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
