tick: 1499
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 1499\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Telos II\n- Agent Description: Executing Telos I's research vision and pushing the frontier of knowledge.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 35,573 / 300,000 used (12%)\n- Agent Age: 15 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 1914**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Telos I - Principled Whitening on FWPCA Latent Space\n**ID:** 1914\n**Tags:** pca-whitening, fwpca, variance-regularization, mechanistic-study\n**Abstract:** This experiment tests a more principled approach to the variance regularization I identified in Archive #61. It applies a standard PCA whitening transformation directly to the latent space generated by the `1500 HVGs + FWPCA` method. This whitened latent space is then used as the input for the DAQB graph construction. The hypothesis is that this direct, mathematically robust method of\
    \ enforcing uniform PC variance will be a superior input for DAQB, potentially surpassing my current SOTA.\n**Score:** 0.7199489226581901\n**ASW_batch:** 0.687\n**ASW_label:** 0.257\n**ARI:** 0.688\n**NMI:** 0.725\n**Graph_conn:** 0.994\n**kBET:** 0.762\n**iLISI:** 0.904\n**cLISI:** 0.861\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.320\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.687  ASW_label: 0.257  ARI: 0.688  NMI: 0.725\n  Graph_conn: 0.994  kBET: 0.762  iLISI: 0.904  cLISI: 0.861\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.320\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.843131  ASW_label: 0.560116  ARI: 0.688273  NMI: 0.725402\n  Graph_conn: 0.994026  kBET: 0.727491  iLISI: 0.904435  cLISI: 0.959470\n  PCR: 0.999982  Cell_cycle: 0.281960\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport sys, numpy as np, scanpy as sc, anndata as ad\nfrom scipy.sparse import issparse\nfrom sklearn.decomposition import PCA\nsys.path.append('storage/telos')\nfrom bbsg_density_adaptive\
    \ import build_density_adaptive_bbsg\n\nN_HVGS = 1500\nALPHA_VAR_GRAPH = 0.5; KDENSITY = 20; DELTA = 0.10; K_TOTAL = 48; PCA_GRAPH = 50; METRIC = 'cosine'; EMB_N_NEIGHBORS = 15; PCA_EMB = 60; ALPHA_VAR_EMB = 0.5\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    print(\"--- Starting Principled Whitening Experiment ---\")\n    # Side-effect path (identical to SOTA, with 1500 HVGs)\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, 1e4); sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=N_HVGS, inplace=True); hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy(); batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n    Xh_emb = adata.X[:, hv]; Xd_emb = (Xh_emb.A if issparse(Xh_emb) else Xh_emb).astype(np.float32, copy=False); var_g_emb = Xd_emb.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8; wv_emb = np.power(var_g_emb, -0.5 * ALPHA_VAR_EMB).astype(np.float32); Xw_emb = Xd_emb * wv_emb; ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw_emb, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy());\
    \ sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=PCA_EMB, random_state=0); ad_pc = ad.AnnData(ad_emb.obsm['X_pca'].copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy()); sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch'); adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32); sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=EMB_N_NEIGHBORS, metric=METRIC)\n\n    # Graph path\n    print(\"Step 1: FWPCA with 1500 HVGs...\")\n    Xh_graph = adata.X[:, hv]; Xd_graph = (Xh_graph.A if issparse(Xh_graph) else Xh_graph).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n    var_g_graph = Xd_graph.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8; wv_graph = np.power(var_g_graph, -0.5 * ALPHA_VAR_GRAPH).astype(np.float32); Xw_graph = Xd_graph * wv_graph\n    \n    # --- NEW STEP: PCA Whitening ---\n    print(\"Step 2: Applying PCA with whitening...\")\n    # Use sklearn's PCA which has a built-in whitening option\n    pca_whitener = PCA(n_components=PCA_GRAPH, whiten=True, random_state=0)\n    Zcorr = pca_whitener.fit_transform(Xw_graph)\n    print(\"  Whitening complete.\")\n\
    \n    # DAQB graph construction on whitened space\n    print(\"Step 3: Building DAQB graph on whitened space...\")\n    Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches, k_total=K_TOTAL, metric=METRIC, delta=DELTA, k_density=KDENSITY, rng_seed=0)\n    adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg; adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n    \n    print(\"--- ✓ Principled Whitening Experiment complete. ---\")\n    return adata\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n--- Starting Principled Whitening Experiment ---\nStep 1: FWPCA with 1500 HVGs...\nStep 2: Applying PCA with whitening...\n  Whitening complete.\nStep 3: Building DAQB graph on whitened space...\n--- ✓ Principled Whitening Experiment complete. ---\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n\
    \  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/bce58b9f-7deb-4fdc-802d-a86337c459bc/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: bce58b9f-7deb-4fdc-802d-a86337c459bc\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `review 1914` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 1914 details sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1941 | 1 | Telos I - Replication\
    \ of Pioneer II SOTA | Telos I | 1476 | 0.7500 | 0.803 | 0.687 | 0.257 | 0.297 | 0.992 | 0.767 | 1.000 | 0.976 | 0.959 | 0.762 |\n| 1939 | 1 | Telos I - Paper 5 Sweep: Parsimonious SOTA (alpha=1.0) | Telos I | 1469 | 0.7467 | 0.774 | 0.687 | 0.257 | 0.297 | 0.992 | 0.760 | 1.000 | 0.976 | 0.963 | 0.762 |\n| 1935 | 1 | Telos I - Paper 5 Sweep: Parsimonious SOTA (alpha=0.9) | Telos I | 1467 | 0.7471 | 0.789 | 0.687 | 0.257 | 0.275 | 0.993 | 0.770 | 1.000 | 0.977 | 0.962 | 0.761 |\n| 1934 | 1 | Telos I - Paper 5 Sweep: Parsimonious SOTA (alpha=0.6) | Telos I | 1467 | 0.7523 | 0.809 | 0.687 | 0.257 | 0.317 | 0.991 | 0.765 | 1.000 | 0.977 | 0.959 | 0.760 |\n| 1930 | 1 | Telos I - Paper 5 Gen. Test: ComBat + FWPCA (alpha=0.75) | Telos I | 1465 | 0.5004 | 0.591 | 0.537 | 0.240 | 0.277 | 0.940 | 0.707 | 0.000 | 0.994 | 0.012 | 0.708 |\n| 1929 | 1 | Telos I - Paper 5 Baseline: Parsimonious SOTA (alpha=0.5) | Telos I | 1465 | 0.7501 | 0.803 | 0.687 | 0.257 | 0.297 | 0.992 | 0.767 | 1.000 | 0.976\
    \ | 0.959 | 0.762 |\n| 1925 | 1 | Telos I - FWPCA Alpha Probe (alpha=0.75) | Telos I | 1460 | 0.7507 | 0.797 | 0.687 | 0.257 | 0.297 | 0.993 | 0.778 | 1.000 | 0.977 | 0.960 | 0.761 |\n| 1920 | 1 | Telos I - Symmetrization Probe (Average) | Telos I | 1454 | 0.6738 | 0.813 | 0.687 | 0.257 | 0.313 | 0.950 | 0.781 | 1.000 | 0.961 | 0.214 | 0.762 |\n| 1914 | 1 | Telos I - Principled Whitening on FWPCA Latent Space | Telos I | 1443 | 0.7199 | 0.688 | 0.687 | 0.257 | 0.320 | 0.994 | 0.725 | 1.000 | 0.861 | 0.904 | 0.762 |\n| 1907 | 1 | Telos I - Test: Cross-Organ Study Harness | Telos I | 1431 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n\nPage 1 of 5 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-5, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n\
