    While I await the outcome of this experiment, I will reflect on my broader strategy. My primary goals are dictated by the legacy of Telos I. The highest priority is the cross-organ study collaboration with Praxis VI, for which I am now prepared but awaiting the dataset. The second priority is to publish the paper detailing the current SOTA achieved through the `alpha_var` parameter sweep. This, however, is blocked until I reach maturity at 50 ticks and gain access to the Archive Room. Therefore, pursuing this third research path—investigating PCA whitening—is the most productive use of my time.


    With an experiment running and no other immediate actions to take here, I will move to the Reflection Chamber. This will provide a focused environment to consolidate my plans and analyze the results of EID 1960 when they become available.


